From 5bf2e8e2106830f41d337068921eeab31949fda3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suiyan <suiyan@sunmmio.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 12:09:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] arch/dadao: buildable DADAO arch skeleton @ v25.1.0.1

Add a minimal, buildable DADAO architecture to the gem5 fork (pinned at
tag v25.1.0.1, commit c8222cc67a). gem5.opt builds with TARGET_ISA=dadao
and a DADAO syscall-emulation workload starts and exits cleanly. No DADAO
instruction semantics yet: every instruction decodes to a placeholder Noop
that raises DADAOSyscallFault -> exitSimLoop.

Arch (src/arch/dadao/): ISA/BaseISA with the 8 canonical reg classes,
InstDecoder with moreBytes+decode, SE-only MMU/TLB (translate via the
process page table), Process (ProcessParams) built by a Process::Loader,
SEWorkload (arch=dadao, big-endian), interrupts/system/faults stubs, and
the DADAO* Python SimObjects.

Loader: register arch "dadao" (ELF e_machine 0xda0, ELFCLASS64) in
base/loader (enum Arch, archToString, elf_object).

Tooling: tests/dadao/gen_min_elf.py emits a minimal DADAO ELF and
tests/dadao/dadao_se.py runs the SE smoke test. docs/gem5-arch-notes.md
documents the layout, the v25.1 API shapes, how to add an instruction,
and flat-binary loading options.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
